      "role": "solo",
      "startDate": "2026-03",
      "endDate": "Present",
      "awards": [],
      "coverImage": "/images/projects/astana-buildings/intro.webp",
      "context": "Pet project about visualizing Astana through buildings.",
      "idea": "Idea come from the existing project https://kontikimaps.com/how-old/helsinki. I wanted to create something similar for my city - Astana. But it turned out to be a disaster...",
      "design": "Dark, cold, steppe design. Gold represents steppe, cold vibes show how could it can be in steppe.",
      "inspiration": "Kontiki projects - How old is this building",
      "process": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "title": "OSM Data Preparation",
          "description": "I started by downloading buildings from geofabrik (OSM distributor). Next step is to find any source where I could take data. But it turned out that there's no centralized data with information about buildings. Th attempt to contact local city halls, companies responsible for urban development in Astana, and other relevant people from industry was not successful. The decision was rough but simple. Collect all possible information. The data was collected through selling appartement portals and Google earth pro. So methodology is a really weak point of this project. But I can ensure that data collected is relatively accurate."
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "title": "Map Styling & Interactivity",
          "description": "I started collecting data long time ago. But only recently I was able to start on online map to share it with people. The original ideas expanded to not just construction year of buildings, but has a lot of other information in different formats, including green urban assessment, crime rates, etc. More proud to add 3D model of Kabanbay Mausoleum that we developed with my friend Tolegen.",
          "image": "/images/projects/astana-buildings/kabanbai-model.webp"
        }
      ],
      "outcome": "Published as a live interactive map. Demonstrates full vector tile pipeline: OpenStreetMap → QGIS → Tippecanoe → PMTiles → MapLibre.",
      "stack": [
